-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",397,{
[12673]="7001C677\n1\tEnter the fight-arena before the fight begins. Do not leave the bounds\tThe fight-arena is the lowered floorspace in the centre of the arena, marked by green banners. The dwarf-club is in your inventory. Gísli Strongclub has given you an excellent weapon with which to earn your prize. You should enter the fight-arena below while wielding your mighty dwarf-club. WARNING: If you leave the fight-arena after entering, you will drop your club. The club may not be used outside of the fight-arena's bounds. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tSlot the dwarf-club in your skills and wait for the fight to begin\tThe fight-arena's bounds are in the centre of the ale-hall at Thorin's Hall, marked by green banners. You should wait for the fight to begin. WARNING: If you leave the arena's bounds after entering, you will drop your mighty dwarf-club. The dwarf-club cannot be used outside of the arena's bounds. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tCollect the glorious beer before the others get the last of it\030Give fellow competitors a whack for good measure (total: 8)\tCompetitors in the lowered fight-arena wish to steal the glorious beer for themselves. Give the greedy folks around you a few good whacks for their impertinence! You must now do whatever it takes to collect the glorious beer, but beware -- if you leave the fight-arena for any reason, you will be disqualified. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tTalk to Gísli Strongclub before the time expires\tGísli Strongclub is in the arena at Thorin's Hall. You should speak with Gísli Strongclub to boast of your excellence in collecting the glorious beer. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[12674]="7002ACA0\n1\tEnter the fight-arena before the fight begins. Do not leave the bounds\tThe fight-arena is the lowered floorspace in the centre of the arena, marked by green banners. The dwarf-club is in your inventory. Gísli Strongclub has given you an excellent weapon to use during the contest. You should enter the fight-arena below while wielding your mighty dwarf-club. WARNING: If you leave the fight-arena after entering, you will drop your club. The club may not be used outside of the fight-arena's bounds. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tSlot the dwarf-club in your skills and wait for the fight to begin\tThe fight-arena's bounds are in the centre of the ale-hall at Thorin's Hall, marked by green banners. You should wait for the fight to begin. WARNING: If you leave the arena's bounds after entering, you will drop your mighty dwarf-club. The dwarf-club cannot be used outside of the arena's bounds. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tGive fellow competitors a whack for good measure (total: 8)\tShow everyone that you are a mighty competitor, give the other participants a good whack and send them reeling! Some competitors may stop moving to take the glorious beer, knock them away while you can, but beware -- if you leave the fight-arena for any reason, you will be disqualified. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tTalk to Gísli Strongclub before the time expires\tGísli Strongclub is in the arena at Thorin's Hall. You should speak with Gísli Strongclub to boast of your excellence in collecting the glorious beer. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[12675]="70014BB6\n1\tRepair gears on Menem-berej (total: 8)\tThe gear-wheels are on the platform of Menem-berej in the centre of the Silvertine Lodes. Thalfar asked you to repair the gears on the platform of Menem-berej.\n2\tReturn to Thalfar\tThalfar is at the camp at the centre of the Silvertine Lodes, overlooking Menem-berej. You should return to Thalfar.\n",
[12676]="7000D3CF\n1\tDefeat Iron Crown warriors (total: 8)\030Defeat Iron Crown crossbowmen (total: 6)\tIron Crown warriors and crossbowmen can be found in the neighbourhood beyond the arch east of Una's allies. Artagan wants you to undermine Muiráthakh's rule in Donnvail by defeating his servants.\n2\tTalk to Artagan\tArtagan is in the city of Donnvail, among Una's allies. You have defeated many of Muiráthakh's servants and should bring news of your success to Artagan.\n",
[12677]="700033DA\n1\tFind Bersi\tBersi is probably at or near the spider-lair north and east of Kheledûl. Nithi has asked you to seek out his friend Bersi who went to gather herbs near a lair of vicious spiders. He recommended that you head north-east before you reach Kheledûl so as not to risk an encounter with the Dourhands.\n",
[12678]="7004CE29\n1\tFind Thorlind on the path south of Felegoth\tThorlind can be found on the path south of Felegoth. You should find Thorlind.\n2\tTalk to Thorlind\tThorlind can be found on the path south of Felegoth. You should talk to Thorlind.\n",
[12679]="70061F76\n1\tAsk if anyone in Herne has seen Cai\tWenna's son Cai has gone missing, but perhaps one of her neighbours has seen him. She wants you to ask around to see if the boy is with them. Wenna's neighbours are located in Herne.\n2\tTalk to Rodric\tMoll stated that she saw Cai sleepwalking and told you to confirm her story with her father. Moll's father Rodric is in the Inn at Herne.\n3\tTalk to Gurthern\tRodric suggested that you should ask the Dunlending Gurthern whether he has seen the missing child. Gurthern has a room upstairs, in the inn in Herne.\n",
[12680]="700001D7\n1\tCollect Jagged Relic-fragment (total: 4)\tSnow-lurkers can be found near the source of the Bruinen and drifts of snow in the area may also hold the jagged relic fragments sought by Deluros. Scholar Deluros has asked you to collect jagged relic fragments from near the source of the Bruinen so he may reassemble the vase so readily dismissed by Glorenglir.\n2\tBring jagged relic fragments to Deluros\tScholar Deluros is in the library of the House of Elrond in Rivendell. You have retrieved some jagged relic fragments. Perhaps Deluros can use them to reassemble the ancient vase.\n",
[12681]="7006C978\n1\tFind the missing goatherd\tLook near Jirush, to the south-east of Western Khanâg, for the missing goatherd.\n2\tLook for the goatherd\tYou have found goats near Jirush. You should look for the goatherd.\n3\tFind the nearby brigand camp\tNear Jirush, you have found goats without a goatherd. Was he harmed by brigands, as Zidek feared? You should find the camp Zidek mentioned.\n4\tDefeat Khûdi toughs (total: 4)\030Free Ubdun\tYou have found the brigand camp, and saw that they are holding a prisoner. You should defeat the brigands and free their prisoner.\n5\tTalk to Ubdun\tYou have defeated the brigands and freed their prisoner, Ubdun the goatherd. You should return to where you saw the goats near Jirush and talk to Ubdun.\n6\tTalk to Zidek in Western Khanâg\tYou have freed Ubdun from being taken prisoner by brigands. He has returned to tend his goats and asked you to talk to Zidek in Western Khanâg.\n",
[12682]="7006556D\n1\tSearch the hillside for caves\tAtharon has suggested that Rendis may be hiding out in a nearby cave. You should search the forest west of Imloth Melui.\n2\tSearch for Rendis\tWhile searching the hills west of Imloth Melui, you have come across a cave-mouth. You should explore the cave for any sign of Rendis or her books.\n3\tReturn to Brunil\tRendis has been found and has promised to return to the city of Imloth Melui. She has asked you to inform Brunil of her whereabouts and plans. Brunil is in the Halls of Healing, in Imloth Melui.\n",
[12683]="70002E45\n1\tUse Calenthon's whistle on the southern slope\tThe slope south of Calenthon would be an ideal location at which to blow the whistle he gave you to summon Malloval. Calenthon gave you a whistle with which to summon his falcon, Malloval.\n2\tLocate Malloval\030Use Calenthon's whistle on the southern slope\tThe ruins are above Calenthon's camp, which can be reached by taking the path north and east from Calenthon's camp. After using Calenthon's whistle, you heard a falcon cry above the ruins near the bridge of Thoniant in Nan Tornaeth.\n3\tThe presence of wights and Corcur together suggests that the Hill-men are in league with whoever or whatever has raised the Dead. One of the Hill-men may bear an emblem or sigil indicating whom they serve....\t\n",
[12684]="70058357\n1\tSearch for any signs of the scouting party\tThe scouting party was last seen somewhere in central Elderslade. You should search for any signs of the scouting party.\n2\tExamine the blood\tThe scouting party was last seen somewhere in central Elderslade. You should examine the blood.\n3\tFollow the trail of blood\tThe scouting party was last seen somewhere in central Elderslade. You should follow the trail of blood.\n4\tFind whoever is responsible for this terrible act\tShakal-atrâd can be found in central Elderslade. You should find who ever is responsible for killing the members of the scouting party.\n5\tDefeat Rásmar Blood-rue\tRásmar Blood-rue can be found in Shakal-atrâd. You should defeat Rásmar Blood-rue.\n6\tReport back to Lóssi at Annâk-khurfu\tLóssi can be found at Annâk-khurfu. You should report back to Lóssi.\n",
[12685]="70028EF5\n1\tTalk to Ianto in Avardin\tIanto is in Avardin, in the central Starkmoor. Levelha asked you to speak to Ianto and convince him to return to work.\n2\tTalk to Levelha in Avardin\tLevelha is in Avardin, in the central Starkmoor. Levelha will be pleased to hear Ianto is returning to work.\n",
[12686]="7002C6E8\n1\tCollect Ithamar's missing trinket\tIthamar believes that he lost his trinket in a skirmish that took place south-west of the road that leads east to Stangard. Ithamar would like for you to find his missing trinket and return it to him at the Cuthstan-camp.\n2\tReturn the trinket to Ithamar at the Cuthstan-camp\tIthamar can be found at the Cuthstan-camp in Wailing Hills. Ithamar waits for the return of his treasured trinket.\n",
[12687]="70058733\n1\tSearch for the waggon in Elderslade\tThe waggon is somewhere on the main road in Elderslade. You should search for the waggon.\n2\tMake a closer inspection of the waggon\tThe waggon is on the main road in Elderslade. You should more closely inspect the waggon.\n3\tDefend the supplies from the raiders\tThe waggon is on the main road in Elderslade. You should defend the supplies from the raiders. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tCollect the supplies (total: 4)\tThe waggon is on the main road in Elderslade. You should collect the supplies.\n5\tBring the supplies to Hertha\tHertha can be found at Shakal-atrâd. You should bring the supplies to Hertha.\n",
[12688]="700529D9\n1\tTalk to Skalla\tSkalla can be found in Vegbár. You should talk to Skalla.\n2\tFind the Beorning scout\tLanghár has asked you to find a way into Goblin-town to disrupt the hobgoblins inside. You should complete 'Watchers at the Gate' and find the Beorning scout near the Goblin-gate.\n3\tEnter Goblin-town by speaking to the Beorning Scout\tThe Beorning scout near the Goblin-gate can escort you into Goblin-town. You should enter Goblin-town to disrupt the hobgoblins' takeover.\n4\tHelp Langhár with 'Interlopers from the North'\030Help Langhár with 'Informing the Masses'\030Help Langhár with 'Thinning Their Ranks'\030Find the hobgoblins' leader\030Help Langhár with 'Watchers at the Gate'\tNow that you have access to the Goblin-town throne room, you should do what you can to interfere with the hobgoblins' efforts there. You should complete quests inside Goblin-town, and find the hobgoblins' leader.\n5\tTalk to Skalla\tSkalla can be found in Vegbár, the Beorning outpost in northern Wolf-denes. You should talk to Skalla.\n",
[12689]="7003ECBD\n1\tSpeak to Glóin in the Misty Mountains\tGlóin has camped out in the Misty Mountains and is trying to deal with the threats present there. Glóin can be found at his camp in the south-west of the Misty Mountains.\n",
[12690]="7001570A\n1\tBring an infused garnet to Mundgeirr\tMundgeirr has asked you to bring him an infused garnet with which he may aid you in bestowing a quality upon your weapon. He does not know, however, where to find such a stone.\n2\tTalk to Mundgeirr to travel to the mithril mine\tMundgeirr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria. Mungeirr has bidden you to talk to him again when you are ready to seek out the forge, but warns you that a vicious band of Orcs and their goblin slaves have taken over the mithril mine.\n3\tBring the empowered garnet to Mundgeirr\tMundgeirr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria. You should return to Mundgeirr to complete the enhancement of your weapon.\n",
[12691]="70042E98\n1\tPick up the empty water barrel\tThe barrel is located next to Anborn in the keep at Bâr Húrin. You should pick up the empty barrel.\n2\tFill the barrel with water\030Fill the barrel with water at the source of the River Gaelos\tThe source of the Gaelos in located just east of Bâr Húrin. You should fill the barrel with water.\n3\tFill water pitchers (total: 8)\tWater pitchers can be found throughout Bâr Húrin. You should fill water pitchers for the Rangers.\n4\tTalk to Anborn\tAnborn can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin. You should talk to Anborn.\n",
[12692]="7004E6C4\n1\tInspect the parchment\tYou should inspect the parchment that Hórin gave you.\n2\tSolve the parchment's riddle\tYou should search in the Grey Mountains for the location hinted at in Hórin's parchment.\n3\tRead the moon-runes\tYou should read the moon-runes on the parchment.\n4\tSolve the parchment's second riddle\tYou should search in the Grey Mountains for the second location, described in moon-runes, on Hórin's parchment.\n5\tRead the moon-runes\tYou should read the moon-runes on the parchment.\n6\tSolve the parchment's third riddle\tYou should search in the Grey Mountains for the third location, described in moon-runes, on Hórin's parchment.\n7\tRead the moon-runes\tYou should read the moon-runes on the parchment.\n8\tLook for a clue in the Glimmerdeep\tThe Glimmerdeep can be found north of Skarháld in the Grey Mountains. You should examine the location in the Glimmerdeep mentioned on Hórin's parchment.\n9\tHórin may be in Skarháld or adventuring with you. You should talk to Hórin.\t\n",
[12693]="70046B1F\n1\tSearch the culverts for the enemy hideout\tThe enemy hideout is in the culverts beneath the ruins of after-battle Osgiliath. You should enter the culverts and find the enemy hideout.\n2\tDefeat foes in the culverts (total: 12)\030Defeat Kamábhil\tThe raiding party hides in the culverts of after-battle Osgiliath. You should defeat the Morgul raiding party.\n3\tReturn to Mablung\tYou should return to Mablung, who can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.\n",
[12694]="700544BD\n1\tGather dust of Morgul-sheen (total: 8)\tDust of Morgul-sheen can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should gather dust of Morgul-sheen.\n2\tBring the dust to Arodor in Barad Orhant\tArodor can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul. You should bring the dust to Arodor.\n",
[12695]="70053E6C\n1\tGather water from a northern tributary into the Morgulduin\030Gather water from a southern tributary into the Morgulduin\030Sample water from a tributary into the Morgulduin\030Sample water from another tributary into the Morgulduin\tThe Morgulduin River runs through Rath Dúath. You should find tributaries into the Morgulduin and sample the water there.\n2\tGather water from the Morgulduin, further upstream\030Sample water from the Morgulduin closer to its source\tThe Morgulduin River runs through Rath Dúath. You should sample the water of the Morgulduin, further upstream, past its tributaries.\n3\tSpeak to Rauniel by the banks of the Morgulduin\tRauniel can be found by the banks of the Morgulduin in northern Rath Dúath. You should speak to the mysterious woman.\n",
[12696]="700157C4\n1\tBring an infused sapphire to Mundgeirr\tMundgeirr has asked you to bring him an infused sapphire through which a quality may be placed upon your weapon. Unfortunately, Mundgeirr does not know exactly where to find such a sapphire.\n2\tSpeak with Mundgeirr to travel to the ancient forge\tMundgeirr can be found in the Dolven-view camp in Moria. Mundgeirr has bidden you to seek out the forge he spoke of, but warns you that a desperate band of morroval-outcasts has taken control of the forge. You should speak with him when you are ready to leave.\n3\tBring the empowered sapphire to Mundgeirr\tMundgeirr can be found at the Dolven-view camp in Moria. You should return to Mundgeirr to complete the enhancement of your weapon.\n",
[12697]="70054684\n1\tTalk to Dolenthol\tDolenthol can be found in Barad Elenath, the Star-gazers' Spire. You should talk to Dolenthol.\n2\tCollect Orders from Ogolúm\030Collect Orders from Durthúl\030Collect Orders from Rhanarch\tFaeron has asked you to find merrevail lieutenants and uncover orders from Lhaereth. You should find and defeat Ogolúm, Durthúl, and Rhanarch within the Circle of Madness.\n3\tTalk to Faeron\tFaeron can be found in Barad Elenath, the Star-gazers' Spire. You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[12698]="7005307D\n1\tExplore the worm-hold of Kidzul-kâlah\030Explore the stone-giant fort\030Explore Gladdenmere isle\030Complete 'Trophies of the Mountain'\030Complete 'Trophies of Stone'\030Complete 'Giants of the Gladdenmere'\030Complete 'Beasts of the Mountain'\030Complete 'Unfortunate Orcs'\tThe wilds of the Gladdenmere rest on the northern edge of the River Gladden. You should explore the wilds of Gladdenmere for Varthmath.\n2\tTalk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere\tVarthmath can be found in the Gladdenmere. You should talk to Varthmath.\n",
[12699]="70038A27\n1\tHelp Grimbold rally his spirits\tGrimbold is at the Fords of Isen in the Westfold. You should help Grimbold to rally his spirits and answer the call to arms once more.\n2\tSpeak with Gandalf\tGandalf is at Erkenbrand's camp in the western Westfold. You should speak with Gandalf.\n",
[12700]="7005AAF6\n1\tFind Mullach Cagar, the Angmarim camp south of Fellgát\tThe Angmarim have made camp south of Fellgát. You should find Mullach Cagar.\n2\tSearch inside the tents at Mullach Cagar\tYou have discovered the Angmarim camp of Mullach Cagar. You should search the camp for clues to the Angmarim's purpose here.\n3\tExamine the mysterious staff on the table in the Angmarim tent\tYou have found a strange staff in Mullach Cagar. You should investigate it more closely.\n4\tDestroy the mysterious staff\tYou have found a mysterious staff in the main tent of Mullach Cagar. You feel it must be a powerful evil artifact. You should destroy the mysterious staff.\n5\tOnce again examine the mysterious staff on the table in the Angmarim tent\tThe staff has completely rebuffed your attack. You should investigate the staff again.\n6\tTake the mysterious staff from the table in the Angmarim tent\tThe mysterious staff cannot be destroyed through any means you currently have at your disposal. You have decided you must take the mysterious staff with you.\n7\tTalk to Hórin in the valley\tYou now have the mysterious staff in your possession. The nausea and paranoia it causes is slowly increasing. You should return to Hórin and Molkha on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.\n",
[12701]="7001A643\n1\tExplore the Drownholt for the source of illness\tNestawen rode upon Alagos on her route to Estolad Mernael. You should explore possible routes Nestawen may have travelled and look for anything out of the ordinary that could have induced the steed's strange illness.\n2\tTalk to Nestawen at Estolad Mernael\tNestawen can be found at Estolad Mernael, the Malledhrim camp in the Drownholt. You should speak with Nestawen immediately and tell her of the particularly fell pool in the Drownholt.\n",
[12702]="70045453\n1\tDefeat Dheghûn (total: 10)\tDheghûn can be found throughout the Drúadan Forest. You should defeat Dheghûn.\n2\tSpeak with Rhûd-pulo-Drât\tRhûd-pulo-Drât can be found in Drû Bhûta. You should speak with Rhûd-pulo-Drât.\n",
[12703]="7004D064\n1\tCollect supplies (total: 5)\tSupplies can be found in Loeglond. You should gather supplies to bait a trap.\n2\tBait the empty supply cart\tThere is an unused supply cart in Loeglond. You should bait the cart with supplies.\n3\tTalk to Sírithon\tYou should talk to Sírithon, who can be found in Loeglond.\n4\tTalk to Sírithon\tYou should talk to Sírithon, who can be found in Loeglond.\n",
[12704]="70028E51\n1\tCollect eggs from crow-nests (total: 10)\tCraban roosting spots can be found in the lands of Pren Gwydh not far from Rook's Hut. You should search for crow-eggs so that Rook may train another flock of crebain from chicks.\n2\tBring the eggs to Rook\tRook is at his hut in Pren Gwydh. You should bring the eggs you collected to Rook in Pren Gwydh.\n",
})
